('21715799-2b84-543b-a5d5-e948683bf5f1'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"At a sawmill, the circumference of the base of a cone-shaped pile of sawdust is 50 ft. The cone rises at an angle of 40°. To the nearest tenth of a foot, how tall is the pile of sawdust? (Note π = 3.14)\n[Figure: cone with a right triangle drawn inside: height dashed, base radius, and a 40° angle at the base edge.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"5.1"},{"key":"B","text":"6.1"},{"key":"C","text":"6.7"},{"key":"D","text":"9.5"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t5.md","source_sha256":"fb0beb8b38f3ff520bee0bf84d567ee65d0b5e7154f4a58335fa388c652dd787","source_question_id":"T5-22","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t5.md (T5-22)."'::jsonb),
