('fefc225a-9f1b-56b5-903b-063c8e5d7fce'::uuid,'est','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In the plane shown in the figure below, lines m and n are cut by transversal line t. The 8 angles at the intersections of these lines are labeled. Which of the following statements, when it is true, CANNOT always be used to prove that lines m and n are parallel?\n[Figure: horizontal lines n (top) and m (bottom) cut by transversal t; at line n, angles numbered 1 (upper left), 2 (upper right), 3 (lower left), 4 (lower right); at line m, 5 (upper left), 6 (upper right), 7 (lower left), 8 (lower right).]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"∠1 ≅ ∠5"},{"key":"G","text":"∠1 ≅ ∠7"},{"key":"H","text":"∠1 ≅ ∠8"},{"key":"J","text":"∠2 ≅ ∠7"},{"key":"K","text":"∠4 ≅ ∠5"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t5.md","source_sha256":"fb0beb8b38f3ff520bee0bf84d567ee65d0b5e7154f4a58335fa388c652dd787","source_question_id":"T5-28","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"}'::jsonb,'"G"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t5.md (T5-28)."'::jsonb),
