('29d99dc8-bb5d-565b-90d7-a524c15db40e'::uuid,'est','"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"For a certain plant, the recommended nighttime temperature range in degrees Fahrenheit is 59° ≤ F ≤ 68°. Given the formula C = (5/9)(F − 32), where C is the temperature in degrees Celsius and F is the temperature in degrees Fahrenheit, what is the corresponding nighttime temperature range in degrees Celsius for the plant?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"0° ≤ C ≤ 5°"},{"key":"G","text":"5° ≤ C ≤ 10°"},{"key":"H","text":"10° ≤ C ≤ 15°"},{"key":"J","text":"15° ≤ C ≤ 20°"},{"key":"K","text":"20° ≤ C ≤ 25°"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t5.md","source_sha256":"fb0beb8b38f3ff520bee0bf84d567ee65d0b5e7154f4a58335fa388c652dd787","source_question_id":"T5-47","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t5.md (T5-47)."'::jsonb),
('388972da-4a3a-5f24-ae84-60d910ad613a'::uuid,'est','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In parallelogram ABCD below, the measure of ∠BCD is 98° and the measure of ∠CDB is 38°. What is the measure of ∠BDA ?\n[Figure: parallelogram ABCD with C top-left, D top-right, B bottom-left, A bottom-right; diagonal BD drawn; angle BCD = 98° at C, angle CDB = 38° at D.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"38°"},{"key":"B","text":"41°"},{"key":"C","text":"44°"},{"key":"D","text":"49°"},{"key":"E","text":"52°"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t5.md","source_sha256":"fb0beb8b38f3ff520bee0bf84d567ee65d0b5e7154f4a58335fa388c652dd787","source_question_id":"T5-48","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t5.md (T5-48)."'::jsonb),
